+| B1 | cal-b, public synthetic row 29 | `dc2514f610252814bc10c4cbec44b2a38382633bf09d057e1084d2740eb4ef76` |
+| C0 | known-signal coupon control | `869f0127586bd49e269083eb8433cceb5b8665e8f9742fd762d886f7a314259e` |
+| C1 | strength-4 known-signal coupon | `bd29e1c4c524c8d7be2628cdc051d389aed8f27c076310f88eb5e79a8410fe5f` |
+
+The evaluator-only file is a plain sheet-ID mapping, separate from the manifest, with SHA-256 `aadeaf11d22c93b588f6d97200c20e65fa7251e3f6c49ce2ae81628299261b86`. A1/B1 use the public synthetic fixture rows 7/29. They are not demo-ledger recipients or sessions and are for N1 study tooling, not the unchanged judge UI.
+
+## Carrier and source invariants
+
+The A/B marked sheets import the existing `nishan.tardos` and `nishan.tardos_carrier` implementations. The carrier is unchanged: `n=1000`, `c=5`, `m=52500`, `block=6`, `dpi=144`, `strength=4.0`, and `epsilon=1e-6`. Both sources have a 55,440-block capacity, so all 52,500 symbols are embedded without shortening.
+
+Only the declared historical header/footer label rectangles are changed before embedding. The shared labels do not falsely claim that a later sheet is unmarked. The frozen original hashes and changed source hashes are recorded in manifest provenance. A Poppler 26.05.0 regression at 144 dpi found zero changed pixels outside those label rectangles for both cal-a and cal-b. The visibly irregular glyph spacing is inherited from the frozen historical PDFs; it is not introduced by packaging or the watermark. It remains intact to preserve the source/carrier invariant. Fresh reserved-study pages use clean stable fonts.
+
+## Diagnostic coupon contract
+
+`diagnostics/coupon_regions.json` has schema `nishan.n1-coupon-regions/v2` and SHA-256 `96acfa720ac2474d9239196f2885137300eaf4345a73b934a3512f2f7d171de2`. It declares C1, control C0, the exact clean C0 reference PNG, five geometry-anchor groups, and nine regions covering 6/12/24-pixel blocks on black/gray/white tones. Each region provides a reference-pixel bbox `[x0,y0,x1,y1]`, source tone, strength 4, and a descriptor-relative hash-bound `.npy` template. Templates are exact `int16` RGB deltas from the clean 144-dpi C1/C0 renders. This is a calibrated known-signal diagnostic, not a Tardos-performance result.
+
+## Verification and visual QA
+
+The final suite passes 25 tests. It covers exact manifest inventory/hashes, A4 one-page geometry, non-escaping paths, matched controls, unchanged carrier parameters, full capacity, plain evaluator-label mapping, coupon descriptor/templates, malformed schema/path/hash rejection, calibration-versus-other-split validation, exclusive deterministic regeneration, source-body pixel preservation, original decoder recovery, Poppler round-trip decoding, hash-bound visual QA, and fail-closed review invalidation when a reviewed PDF hash or required observation differs.
+
+- Original decoder, direct PDFs: A1 and B1 each recover all 52,500 symbols with zero mismatches.
+- Original decoder, clean 144-dpi MuPDF renders: A1 and B1 each recover all 52,500 symbols with zero mismatches.
+- Independent Poppler 26.05.0 round trip: A1 has 74 mismatches (`0.001409524` BER) and accuses exactly row 7; B1 has 10 mismatches (`0.000190476` BER) and accuses exactly row 29.
+- Final Poppler renders of A0, A1, B0, B1, C0, and C1 were inspected individually at 144 dpi. Labels are truthful, content is legible, and no new clipping or overlap was observed. The render records are bound to the exact six inspected PDF hashes in `qa/visual_inspection.json`; different regenerated bytes produce `needs_visual_review` rather than inheriting a pass.
+- The independent Task 3 strict pack validator accepts this exact manifest and validates the direct labels, all sheet/source and optional path/hash pairs, exhaustive artifact inventory, changed-source provenance, coupon reference/templates, and metadata shapes.
+
+Canon's normal A4 printable-area model leaves 49,213 selected symbols fully inside the nominal printable area and 3,287 intersecting the nominal unprintable margin. The carrier extent remains `[0,0,1188,1680]` at 144 dpi. No shrink, reflow, crop, strength change, borderless mode, or Fit-to-Page compensation is applied. Physical edge loss is an explicit measured outcome.
