+# N1 calibration print and capture guide
+
+This is a calibration pack, not a result. Print the six files in the order below, keep the evaluator label file private until the receiver preparation commitment exists, and return the original camera files. Do not change scale to make the carrier fit the printer margins.
+
+## Before printing
+
+1. Use the Canon G2020 and one batch of A4 plain paper for all six sheets.
+2. In the print dialog select **A4**, **Plain Paper**, **Actual size / 100%**, and normal one-page printing.
+3. Turn **Borderless printing OFF**. Turn **Fit-to-Page / Scale to fit OFF**. Turn **Economy / toner-save OFF**.
+4. Record the exact driver choices shown for print quality and colour below. Driver wording varies, so do not translate a displayed setting into a guessed DPI.
+5. The carrier's 144 DPI value is its PDF render coordinate system. It is not a Canon driver setting and is not a hardware-DPI choice to find in the dialog.
+
+Canon documents that Fit-to-Page enlarges or reduces the page. Canon also documents that borderless printing enlarges the image and can crop its edges. Neither is suitable here. With ordinary non-borderless A4 printing, Canon lists a 203.2 x 289.0 mm printable area: approximately 3.4 mm at each side, 3.0 mm at the top, and 5.0 mm at the bottom. The unchanged full-page carrier reaches those normally unprintable margins, so some edge modulation may be absent. That loss is an intended measurement; do not shrink, reflow, crop, or re-embed the PDFs to hide it.
+
+Primary Canon references:
+
+- [G2020 print area](https://ij.manual.canon/ij/webmanual/Manual/All/G2020%20series/EN/UG/ug-195.html)
+- [G2020 standard-size printable areas](https://ij.manual.canon/ij/webmanual/Manual/All/G2020%20series/EN/UG/ug-196.html)
+- [G2020 Fit-to-Page behaviour](https://ij.manual.canon/ij/webmanual/PrinterDriver/W/G2020%20series/1.0/EN/PPG/dg-c_fit.html)
+
+## File-to-sheet map
+
+Print exactly one named file at a time. A0/A1 deliberately look alike, as do B0/B1. As soon as each page leaves the printer, turn it over and write only its sheet ID (`A0` through `C1`) lightly in pencil on the **back**. Never write, stamp, attach a label, or add any mark to the tested front. The marked/control identity belongs in the filename, this run sheet, and that back-of-page handling label.
+
+| Order | File | Sheet | What it is |
+| ---: | --- | --- | --- |
+| 1 | `sheets/A0.pdf` | A0 | Core source A, unmarked control |
+| 2 | `sheets/A1.pdf` | A1 | Core source A, public synthetic marked calibration sheet |
+| 3 | `sheets/B0.pdf` | B0 | Core source B, unmarked control |
+| 4 | `sheets/B1.pdf` | B1 | Core source B, public synthetic marked calibration sheet |
+| 5 | `sheets/C0.pdf` | C0 | Diagnostic coupon, unmarked control |
+| 6 | `sheets/C1.pdf` | C1 | Diagnostic coupon, strength-4 known-signal regions |
+
+The exact source references are `sources/cal-a.pdf`, `sources/cal-b.pdf`, and `sources/cal-c.pdf`. C0/C1 are diagnostic coupons only: they are not full Tardos pages, do not represent 52,500-symbol results, and have no expected guilty recipient.
+
+The A and B pages are historical calibration fixtures, not newly typeset or judge-facing documents. Their frozen originals contain visibly irregular glyph spacing. N1 packaging preserves that inherited body rendering exactly and changes only the declared header/footer label regions before embedding; the 144-dpi Poppler regression requires zero changed pixels elsewhere. Treat those inherited type imperfections as source provenance, not as a new watermark or printer defect. Fresh reserved-study pages use clean stable fonts.
+
+Keep `evaluation_labels.json` evaluator-only. It is not needed to print or photograph the sheets.
+
+### Evaluator-only tooling boundary
+
+After the receiver preparation commitment exists, the evaluator may open the hash-bound `evaluation_labels.json`. It is the only transferable sheet-to-contributor mapping. Its identifiers are research-calibration rows from the fixed public fixture, not recipients or sessions from the current demo ledger, and these sheets must be processed with the N1 study tooling rather than the unchanged judge UI. Never copy a contributor mapping or attack label into a receiver preparation request.
+
+## Record the actual print setup
+
+Fill this in from the driver and paper package before printing:
+
+| Field | Actual value |
+| --- | --- |
+| Printer shown by operating system | Canon G2020 / exact displayed name: __________ |
+| Driver and operating system | __________ |
+| Paper brand, size, weight, batch if shown | __________ |
+| Media type displayed | __________ |
+| Print quality displayed | __________ |
+| Colour / grayscale setting displayed | __________ |
+| Borderless displayed | OFF / exact wording: __________ |
+| Page layout / scaling displayed | Actual size or 100% / exact wording: __________ |
+| Economy / toner-save displayed | OFF / exact wording: __________ |
+| Other colour-management choice shown | __________ |
+| Date, time, and operator | __________ |
+
+If the dialog does not expose one of these controls, write **not shown**. Do not infer it.
+
+## Take 12 original photos
+
+The exact POCO model is currently unknown. Record it from the phone's Settings/About screen; do not guess.
+
+For every sheet, take two photos with the native POCO camera app:
+
+1. `front`: camera square to the page.
+2. `angle`: approximately 20 degrees from the page normal.
+
+Use the same flat support and even lighting for all 12 photos. Keep all four paper corners visible, fill the frame while retaining the corners, focus on the page, use no filter or beauty/document enhancement, and keep flash/exposure choices consistent and recorded. Retake immediately if text is not readable or a corner is missing. A full-page original should be at least 1600 pixels wide.
+
+Suggested pairing log:
+
+| Sheet | Front original filename | Approx. 20-degree original filename | Retakes / notes |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| A0 | __________ | __________ | __________ |
+| A1 | __________ | __________ | __________ |
+| B0 | __________ | __________ | __________ |
+| B1 | __________ | __________ | __________ |
+| C0 | __________ | __________ | __________ |
+| C1 | __________ | __________ | __________ |
+
+Do not edit, enhance, resize, or re-save the 12 camera files. A separate duplicate on the sender's device is not required before transfer; leave the acquisition files in the phone's camera storage until receipt is confirmed. The simplest conservative delivery is to place the originals in one ZIP archive and send the ZIP using **WhatsApp Document**. Alternatively, send each original individually using **Document**. Do not send them with the normal **Photo** action.
+
+Record hashes at the sender if practical and again at intake. A `.zip` or Document filename alone does not prove byte identity or unchanged pixels: without a matching sender hash or equivalent ZIP evidence, classify identity as **declared / unverified**, not verified. Ordinary messaging-photo transfer, document transport, scanner continuous-tone output, and scanner bilevel output are different categories and must remain separately named and paired to the same original. Messaging/scanner derivatives can be collected later. A scanner and a second phone are not required for this six-sheet calibration.
+
+## Build and verify the transferable pack
+
+From the repository root, with the shared environment left read-only:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=2 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 MKL_NUM_THREADS=2 NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS=2 PYTHONPATH="$PWD/prototypes/nishan_pq:$PWD" __PRIVATE_CAPTURE_WORKSPACE__/SIH/.venv/bin/python -m research.n1_v2.build_pack --output /path/to/new-pack
+```
+
+The output path must not already exist. To verify an existing pack without changing it:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=2 OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 MKL_NUM_THREADS=2 NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS=2 PYTHONPATH="$PWD/prototypes/nishan_pq:$PWD" __PRIVATE_CAPTURE_WORKSPACE__/SIH/.venv/bin/python -m research.n1_v2.build_pack --verify /path/to/pack
+```
+
+`manifest.json` is the mandatory file-to-sheet map and contains the SHA-256 hash of every transferable artifact. Do not print if verification reports a mismatch.
